# Line endings, pinned rather than left to each machine's git config.
#
# Without this file, a Windows checkout with the common `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites text
# files to CRLF on the way out of git. That is usually harmless. Here it is not, because two
# things in this repository are compared byte-for-byte:
#
#   docs/cli.md   is generated by cmd/gen-docs, and TestReferenceIsCurrent asserts the
#                 generated bytes equal the committed bytes. The generator emits LF. A CRLF
#                 checkout fails that test with zero line-content differences and a length
#                 delta exactly equal to the number of lines — which reads like a stale file
#                 and is not one. Measured on a real Windows machine, 2026-08-13.
#
#   packaging/libkrun-windows/patches/*.patch  must apply exactly. `git apply` is offered no
#                 fuzz on purpose, so that a drifted pin fails loudly; line endings rewritten
#                 underneath it would make that failure mean something else entirely.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `text=auto` alone: auto only normalises what git stores, and still
# hands Windows CRLF in the working tree, which is where both problems above happen.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files whose contents are their own format and must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.erofs binary
*.tar.gz binary
